{% comment %}
  What the reviews wave has to do to the section behind it.

  This used to set the quote under the wave as well, reaching across with
  ":has(.wave-divider--reviews) + .shopify-section" - which meant the quote's
  formatting depended on the two sections staying adjacent and in order. The
  quote is sections/review-quote.liquid now and sets itself, so all that is
  gone and only the rule below is left, which is genuinely about the wave.

  The "Reviews ·" label is not a section either: it's set along the inside of
  the curve in wave-divider.liquid.

  Rendered from the wave section's custom Liquid block, next to the divider.
{% endcomment %}

{% stylesheet %}

  /* This section stands its own background down.

     The ingredient section above bleeds its spice backdrop downwards so the
     artwork runs under this wave rather than stopping on a straight line
     above it. That bleed sits behind this section, and this section's
     background - later in the DOM at the same z-index - would paint straight
     over it. Only the area above the curve is affected: the wave's own fill
     is opaque, so the band below it is untouched. */
  #MainContent > div.shopify-section:has(.wave-divider--reviews) .section-background {
    background-color: transparent;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
